        "target_title": "fix(config): use host key only as a fallback",
        "created_at": "2026-10-19T03:41:38.135Z",
        "note": {
          "id": 4039344382,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "**suggestion (non-blocking):** When a config-file `host` matches no remote, glab now switches to the remote's host without saying so. That's the intended behavior, but a user who expected the configured instance (for example, someone not signed in to gitlab.com, in a repository whose only remote is on gitlab.com) gets a 401/404 with no hint that the configured `host` was set aside. A debug line here would make that easy to spot with `GLAB_DEBUG=true`:\n\n```go\ndbg.Debug(\"config host \" + hostOverride + \" matches no git remote; resolving from remotes instead\")\n```\n\n`dbg` is already used in `factory.go`.",
          "author": {
            "id": 11809982,
            "username": "jay_mccure",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Jay McCure",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/11809982/avatar.png?v=1792376207",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jay_mccure"
