      {
        "id": 6153736615,
        "project_id": 34675721,
        "action_name": "commented on",
        "target_id": 4039301590,
        "target_iid": 4039301590,
        "target_type": "Note",
        "author_id": 21826781,
        "target_title": "fix(govern): keep audit event batches within GitLab's limits",
        "created_at": "2026-10-19T03:22:54.732Z",
        "note": {
          "id": 4039301590,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I finished my review and found nothing to comment on. Nice work! :tada:\n\n- The wait seam was the only change since my last review. It is now a `waitFor` field on `options` with an `options.wait` method, and no package-level var is left. That addresses my earlier thread.\n- `options.wait` returns `ctx.Err()` on cancellation and otherwise waits on `time.After(d)`. The new cancellation test covers this and is correct.\n- `recordWaits(opts)` is called before each use in the rate-limit tests. Each subtest has its own `tt` and `opts`, so the per-test recording is safe.\n- The hook case in `TestSyncSession_ByCaller` still fails fast and posts nothing. The manual case waits through the stubbed seam and posts 1 event. Both match the intended behavior.\n- I found no new correctness problems in the lines added since my last review.",
          "author": {
            "id": 21826781,
            "username": "GitLabDuo",
            "public_email": null,
            "name": "GitLab Duo",
